--- ADDITIONAL FIX (appended): transmit-timeout units bug ---

esp32_can_send()'s bounded-timeout branch compares an elapsed
MICROsecond count (mp_hal_ticks_us) against `timeout_ms`, which is a
MILLIsecond value everywhere else (it is handed to pdMS_TO_TICKS in the
line above). Every timeout therefore expired about 1000x early:
`send(..., timeout=200)` gave up after 200us, far less than the time to
put a single frame on a 50kbit/s bus, so nearly every transmit raised
ETIMEDOUT even though the frame had been queued successfully.

Observed on hardware before this fix: a constant stream of
"TWAI send failed ... ESP_ERR_TIMEOUT", poll reads never marked as sent
(so the scheduler retried them forever), and enough console output to
visibly slow the GUI. Until this patch is built in, twai_driver.py
deliberately passes NO timeout -- see its send() comment.

--- a/src_can_v2/mod_can.c	2026-09-06 00:25:32.701305389 +0330
+++ b/src_can_v2/mod_can.c	2026-09-06 00:25:32.717475014 +0330
@@ -601,7 +601,16 @@
             check_esp_err(twai_transmit_v2(self->handle, &tx_msg, pdMS_TO_TICKS(timeout_ms)));           
             while (self->last_tx_success < 0) {
                 if (timeout_ms != portMAX_DELAY) {
-                    if (mp_hal_ticks_us() - start >= timeout_ms) {
+                    /* tbgw patch: `start` is in MICROseconds
+                     * (mp_hal_ticks_us) but `timeout_ms` is a
+                     * MILLIsecond value -- it is passed to
+                     * pdMS_TO_TICKS() just above. Comparing the two
+                     * directly made every timeout expire ~1000x early:
+                     * send(..., timeout=200) gave up after 200us, far
+                     * less than one frame at 50kbit/s, so virtually
+                     * every transmit raised ETIMEDOUT despite having
+                     * been queued successfully. Scale to microseconds. */
+                    if (mp_hal_ticks_us() - start >= timeout_ms * 1000) {
                         mp_raise_OSError(MP_ETIMEDOUT);
                     }
                 }
